   "subject": "Re: Two dimensional GPCM estimation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I assume your other model is a confirmatory item factor analysis model, so I&#39;ll respond under that assumption. <div><br></div><div>In general, I wouldn&#39;t treat exploratory factor models in the same way as confirmatory ones. The former are highly over-parameterized and subject to rotational indeterminacy, so the correlation will be a function of what rotation you pick and under what criteria. EFAs are largely meant to be suggestive of underlying factor patterns and relationships but not definitive. HTH.<div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, May 11, 2023 at 4:26 PM Yanxuan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">xiaoqi...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
